From: Azra Bano <azrabano.work@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:02:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Floor the linesearch gradient tolerance at the
 derivative's rounding noise.

The linesearch accepts a point when |f'(alpha)| < tolerance*ls_tolerance
(scaled). When that is below the rounding error of f'(alpha), a sum of terms
much larger than the result, the sign of the derivative is noise and the
bracketed search runs until ls_iterations is exhausted. This happens with
tolerance=0, and in single precision with the default tolerance.

Floor the tolerance at eps*sum|terms|, with the magnitudes of the terms of
the derivative accumulated in PrimalPrepare. In double precision with the
default tolerance the floor is inactive.
